================
LACP Security

Why we did this
================
EtherChannel combines multiple physical links into a single logical link.

LACP (Link Aggregation Control Protocol) is the industry-standard protocol used to dynamically form EtherChannels.

Without proper controls:

- Unauthorized links may join the bundle.
- Misconfigured devices may affect traffic flow.
- Rogue switches may attempt to participate in aggregation.
- Traffic loss and instability can occur.

To improve reliability and security, LACP validates channel members before allowing them to join the EtherChannel.

What will happen
================
1. LACP packets are exchanged between devices.
2. Neighbor devices verify compatibility.
3. Only approved interfaces join the bundle.
4. Mismatched ports are rejected.
5. Invalid links remain outside the EtherChannel.
6. Stable and secure aggregation is maintained.

Example

Without LACP
------------

Switch A
   ||
   ||
Switch B

Mode: ON

Result:
--------
No verification
Misconfigurations may occur


With LACP
---------

Switch A
   ||
Port-Channel1
   ||
Switch B

Mode: ACTIVE

Result:
--------
Interfaces validated
Unauthorized links rejected

Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Validates EtherChannel members.
2. Prevents accidental misconfigurations.
3. Improves redundancy.
4. Supports automatic negotiation.
5. Detects mismatched configurations.
6. Industry standard protocol.
7. More secure than Mode ON.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Additional protocol overhead.
2. Requires matching configurations.
3. Troubleshooting may be more complex.
4. Does not encrypt traffic.
5. Does not prevent broadcast storms.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Even after securing EtherChannels with LACP, attackers could still manipulate Cisco proprietary EtherChannel negotiations.

Cisco therefore provides:

PAgP Security

for environments using Cisco's proprietary Port Aggregation Protocol (PAgP).

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Configure LACP

Switch(config)# interface range g0/1-2
Switch(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode active


Configure Secure Port-Channel

Switch(config)# interface port-channel1
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk native vlan 999
Switch(config-if)# switchport nonegotiate


(Optional)

Switch(config)# interface range g0/1-2
Switch(config-if-range)# udld port aggressive


(Optional)

Switch(config)# interface port-channel1
Switch(config-if)# spanning-tree guard root

Verification
============

show etherchannel summary

show lacp neighbor

show lacp internal

show interfaces port-channel 1

